    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172-a1">

                <pb facs="0314" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg226"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 604.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Salisbury to Mr.
                            Lincoln.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am commanded by the Queen, my sovereign,
                    to request you to return to the President of the United States of America Her
                    Majesty’s warmest thanks for the kind expressions of sympathy conveyed through
                    you to Her Majesty, to their Royal Highnesses the Prince and Princess of Wales,
                    and to the royal family, on the occasion of the great sorrow which has fallen
                    upon them, and upon the whole nation, by the death of His Royal Highness the
                    Duke of Clarence and Avondale and Earl of Athlone.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Salisbury.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
